{
  "_note": "The workbench's options: hand-maintained from the ledgers (docs/superpowers/plans/*-ledger.md) and the workbench plan's Global Constraints. ids are app/song/library.h's (sym names the enum; smoke.mjs checks them); a kit from 16 is a workbench preset (wb_drums.h's WB_KIT_*, 16 + its index). status: approved (offered, the dice pick it), candidate (offered, marked; the dice skip it; none among the instruments; a candidate comping style is one the roll weighs 0, held on 2, held on 2 and 4 and light eighths until Sam sets their weights), retired (behind 'show retired'). ride: the kit plays the ride section (the sampled kits). set: a shipped sampled kit's sample set (samples/kits.json, git-ignored: unavailable until tools/prep_kits.py has made it). Families (Sam, 2026-10-29: the synth/acoustic divide applies to drums only): a song's family chooses its kit (the family row swaps the kit, its dice and the lanes' draw stay in the family; electric goes with either); the keys, bass, pad and lead mix freely across families. No ear candy (Sam, 2026-10-29): the instruments that only played it (the music box, the bells, none) have no role. The choir (the formant oo-aah, of any family): a pad a song may draw over its set's (library's lib_song_pad, 1 song in 4), and one of the pad's solo voices, in the vox pad's place (the vox pad retired, 2026-10-31: no patch). The organ is the tonewheel (2026-10-31; electric, as the Rhodes): on the keys the song's drawbars and register; as a pad (its one-stop 4', the scanner chorus by section) a song may draw it over its set's (lib_song_pad, about 1 song in 7, never over organ keys). Leads (Sam, 2026-10-29): the felt piano leads too (never over felt keys), the vibes are the vibraphone (sampled, then modeled from 2026-11-03); the muted trumpet, sax, guitar lick, string lead and cello are retired; the lead instruments are the flute, felt piano, vibes and Knight (lead styles build: the kalimba, saw lead and synth pluck retired, the Emilyguitar on the keys only). An old snapshot's retired lead plays the flute or the vibes in its place (library.c's lib_lead_approved), said on restore. Removed with their models (2026-10-31: no patch, so no role, not even behind 'show retired'): the upright (an old snapshot's bass plays the electric bass: lib_bass_approved, said on restore), the kalimba, saw lead and synth pluck, the music box and the bells. Lead styles (lead styles, 2026-10-31): the lead_style override's values, 2 + leads.h's LS_*; the phrase planner (0) and the hybrid (1) are retired (an old snapshot naming one restores on a rolled style). Generated (tools/patterns/import.py, from patterns/; never edit them here): patterns (a new one named by its file), kickPhrases and strumPats (id: patterns/model.json's; index: the engine table's, which the override row forces). A candidate there plays only when picked; Approve writes patterns/status.json, and tools/patterns/import.sh makes it one the roll draws.",
